		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4851&amp;p=35645#p35645"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>So, I just tried with your codeplug, and the same firmware version, and it works as expected.<br>I'm not sure if you understood how roaming works.<br>If you're static (e.g, not really moving), you should <strong class="text-strong">NOT</strong> define a distance in the "<em class="text-italics">Roaming</em>" option (the one in the QuickMenu settings), but manual instead.<br>Reason is, the re-sorting of the zone will only happen if you moved by, at least, that distance since the last sorting.<br>On the other hand, using "<em class="text-italics">Roaming: Manual</em>" will re-trigger a zone sorting, each time you validate that option (I mean, pressing <strong class="text-strong">GREEN</strong> button while it's selected).<br>Of course, your transceiver location has to be properly set (using GPS or manually enterred) to make it working.</div></blockquote>OK, what are you telling me i didn't found on manual. I used to use Motorola roaming system.<br>Now is clear.<br>Thanks<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=558">IK1HJT</a> — Fri Feb 07, 2025 3:24 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
